> rt1(x: f32) = asfloat(asuint(x))
> idf(x: f32) = x
> equiv rt1 idf
rt1 and idf are equal on the domain of rt1 (proved by SAT: 2733 AIG nodes, 382 conflicts)
> rt2(x: f32) = asfloat(asint(x))
> wrap rt2
wrap analysis of rt2:
  asfloat(asint(x))   (f32)
      nnan not proved: no NaN in the sampled points only
      ninf not proved: no inf in the sampled points only
  end to end vs the real-number result: max abs error 0, max rel error 0, max 0 ulp (correctly rounded)
  sampled 65536 points (domain has 4278190079 points); not exhaustive
> rt3(x: u32) = asuint(asfloat(x))
> wrap rt3
wrap analysis of rt3:
  asfloat(x)   (f32)
      nnan not proved: no NaN in the sampled points only
      ninf not proved: no inf in the sampled points only
  end to end: equals the mathematical (unbounded) result everywhere
  sampled 65536 points (domain has 4294967296 points); not exhaustive
> rt4(x: f32) = asuint(asfloat(asint(x)))
> wrap rt4
wrap analysis of rt4:
  asfloat(asint(x))   (f32)
      nnan not proved: no NaN in the sampled points only
      ninf not proved: no inf in the sampled points only
  end to end: equals the mathematical (unbounded) result everywhere
  sampled 65536 points (domain has 4278190079 points); not exhaustive
> nn(x: f32) = -(-x)
> wrap nn
wrap analysis of nn:
  no wrapping or rounding operations
  end to end vs the real-number result: max abs error 0, max rel error 0, max 0 ulp (correctly rounded)
  sampled 65536 points (domain has 4278190079 points); not exhaustive
> ab(x: f32) = abs(x)
> ab2(x: f32) = x < 0 ? -x : x
> equiv ab ab2 ftz
ab and ab2 differ at 255 points of the sample, e.g. x=-4.91007275e-39: 0 vs -4.91007275e-39
  every float operation flushed subnormals to zero (ftz)
> q1(x: u32) = asfloat(x | 0x7fc00000)
> q2(x: u32) = asfloat(0x7fc00000)
  note: asfloat of an untyped integer: read as u32 -> f32
> equiv q1 q2
q1 and q2 are equal on the domain of q1 (proved by SAT: 54 AIG nodes, 0 conflicts)
> equiv q1 q2 nanbits
q1 and q2 differ at 65533 points of the sample, e.g. x=4294967295: NaN 0xffffffff vs NaN 0x7fc00000
  NaN results compared by their bits, sign and payload (nanbits)
